3. How Responsive Utility Classes and Breakpoints Handle Multi-Device Support
Bootstrap uses responsive breakpoints to adjust layouts according to screen size.
Common Breakpoints:
Breakpoint	Device Type
sm	Small devices
md	Tablets
lg	Laptops
xl	Large screens
Example:
<div class="col-12 col-md-6 col-lg-4">
This means:
•	Full width on mobile 
•	Half width on tablets 
•	One-third width on large screens 
Responsive Utility Classes:
Bootstrap also provides classes like:
•	d-none 
•	d-md-block 
•	text-center 
•	p-3 
These help control visibility, spacing, alignment, and layout for different devices without extra CSS.
Result:
•	Website automatically adapts to phones, tablets, and desktops. 
•	Better user experience on all screen sizes. 
•	Less effort in writing media queries manually. 
