4. Why Form Validation Feedback Improves User Trust on Signup Forms
Form validation checks whether the user enters correct information before submission.
Bootstrap provides built-in validation classes such as:
•	is-valid 
•	is-invalid 
•	valid-feedback 
•	invalid-feedback 
Example:
<input type="email" class="form-control is-invalid">
<div class="invalid-feedback">
  Please enter a valid email.
</div>
Benefits:
•	Users instantly know if input is correct or incorrect. 
•	Reduces form submission errors. 
•	Improves user confidence and trust. 
•	Makes signup process smoother and more professional. 
•	Prevents incomplete or invalid data entry. 
A startup website with proper validation appears more reliable and secure.
