5. How Utility Classes Help Avoid Writing Repetitive CSS
Bootstrap utility classes are small helper classes used for:
•	Margin 
•	Padding 
•	Colors 
•	Alignment 
•	Display properties 
•	Flexbox 
Example:
<div class="text-center mt-4 p-3 bg-light">
Instead of writing:
text-align: center;
margin-top: 20px;
padding: 15px;
background-color: #f8f9fa;
Advantages:
•	Reduces repetitive CSS code. 
•	Speeds up styling process. 
•	Keeps code cleaner and shorter. 
•	Improves consistency throughout the project. 
•	Easier to maintain and modify. 
This is very useful for startups that need rapid UI development.
